issues.body:
Since 1.7.1, you create a new configScreen at mod initialization, however, if any option is changed through the API, the saveConsumer triggers, which for some options might run a levelRenderer.allChanged() which causes a crash with Sodium because it has a mixin hooked there and on mod initialisation, some GL stuff isn't initialized yet.
An easy fix is to check if a level is not null because levelRenderer.allChanged() does nothing if there's no level anyway.

1.7.1:
```java
                .setSaveConsumer(newValue -> {
                    MoreCulling.CONFIG.useBlockStateCulling = newValue;
                    Minecraft mc = Minecraft.getInstance();
                    if (mc != null && mc.levelRenderer != null) {
                        mc.levelRenderer.allChanged();
                    }
                })
```

 Fix:
```java
                .setSaveConsumer(newValue -> {
                    MoreCulling.CONFIG.useBlockStateCulling = newValue;
                    Minecraft mc = Minecraft.getInstance();
                    if (mc != null && mc.level != null && mc.levelRenderer != null) {
                        mc.levelRenderer.allChanged();
                    }
                })
```

